{"id":"756bb8c7ba66537316981bc8d429f0c0f9642654","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/beam","sha":"756bb8c7ba66537316981bc8d429f0c0f9642654","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"CHANGES.md","lines":["@@ -127,6 +127,7 @@"," * (Go) GCS and Dataflow clients now support non-default universes such as Trusted Partner Cloud (TPC), using the universe domain from `GOOGLE_CLOUD_UNIVERSE_DOMAIN` or the default credentials. Added a `--gcs_endpoint` pipeline option to override the GCS endpoint ([#40569](https://github.com/apache/beam/issues/40569))."," * (Java) `GcsUtil` now uses the java-storage client (GcsUtil V2) for GCS operations by default instead of gcsio (GcsUtil V1). To go back to V1, pass `--experiments=disable_gcsutil_v2`. Pipelines with the `use_grpc_for_gcs` experiment keep using V1. The `use_gcsutil_v2` experiment is no longer needed and is now ignored ([#40712](https://github.com/apache/beam/issues/40712))."," * [Beam SQL] Added `PRIMARY KEY (...) NOT ENFORCED` to `CREATE EXTERNAL TABLE`, and `ALTER TABLE ... ADD/DROP PRIMARY KEY` ([#40826](https://github.com/apache/beam/issues/40826)).","+* [Beam SQL] Added a `WITH (...)` clause to set per-statement connector options in `FROM` and `INSERT INTO` ([#40848](https://github.com/apache/beam/issues/40848))."," "," ## Breaking Changes"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"sdks/java/extensions/sql/build.gradle","lines":["@@ -150,8 +150,44 @@ task copyFmppTemplatesFromSrc(type: Copy) {","   from \"src/main/codegen\"","   into \"${project.buildDir}/templates-fmpp/codegen\""," }","+","+// config.fmpp adds Beam's rules to Calcite's grammar, Parser.jj, only at fixed hooks. There is","+// no hook that allows us to add syntax right after a table name, which is needed to set options","+// using WITH ('key' = value, ...). To get around this, the copyFmppTemplatesFromCalciteCore task","+// edits its copy of Parser.jj to add that syntax.","+//","+// Each entry below pairs a snippet of Calcite's grammar, the anchor, with Beam code. The task","+// inserts the code right after the anchor. Take the first entry. TableRef3, Calcite's rule for a","+// table in FROM, contains","+//   [ tableRef = Snapshot(tableRef) ]","+// which parses an optional FOR SYSTEM_TIME AS OF. After the edit, that line reads","+//   [ tableRef = Snapshot(tableRef) ] tableRef = TableClauseOpt(tableRef, TableClause.Role.READ)","+// So right after FOR SYSTEM_TIME AS OF, Beam's TableClauseOpt rule parses an optional WITH clause.","+//","+// The build fails if an anchor is missing from Parser.jj or shows up more than once. This will catch","+// the case when a Calcite upgrade changes one of these snippets. To fix that, find the snippet's new","+// form in Parser.jj and update the anchor below.","+def calciteParserExtensions = [","+  // Parses WITH on a table in FROM. This is the example above.","+  '[ tableRef = Snapshot(tableRef) ]': 'tableRef = TableClauseOpt(tableRef, TableClause.Role.READ)',","+  // Parses WITH on the INSERT target, in Calcite's SqlInsert rule, before the optional column list.","+  '[ LOOKAHEAD(5) tableRef = ExtendTable(tableRef) ]': 'tableRef = TableClauseOpt(tableRef, TableClause.Role.WRITE)',","+  // Beam gives a FROM table with WITH an alias: its own name. If the query gives it an alias too,","+  // keep only the query's. This runs at the end of TableRef3.","+  '[ tableRef = Tablesample(tableRef) ]': '{ tableRef = TableClause.collapseImplicitAlias(tableRef); }',","+  // SQL also uses WITH for common table expressions, as in WITH q AS (...) SELECT * FROM q. A","+  // reference to q can't take WITH options. They would become part of the name, and Calcite would","+  // then look for a catalog table instead of using q. addWith builds every such query, so check","+  // the references there.","+  'JAVACODE SqlNode addWith(SqlNodeList withList, SqlNode e) {': 'TableClause.checkCteReferences(withList, e);',","+  // OrderByLimitOpt attaches the ORDER BY of such a query after addWith has run, so check the","+  // ORDER BY here too.","+  'if (orderBy != null || offsetFetch[0] != null || offsetFetch[1] != null) {': 'TableClause.checkCteReferencesInOrderBy(e, orderBy);',","+]","+"," task copyFmppTemplatesFromCalciteCore(type: Copy) {","   dependsOn configurations.fmppTemplates","+  inputs.property(\"calciteParserExtensions\", calciteParserExtensions)","   File calciteCoreJar = files(configurations.fmppTemplates.files).filter {","     it.name.startsWith(\"beam-vendor-calcite\")","   }.singleFile","@@ -170,6 +206,18 @@ task copyFmppTemplatesFromCalciteCore(type: Copy) {","     line ->","       line.replace('import com.google.common.', 'import org.apache.beam.vendor.calcite.v1_40_0.com.google.common.')","   }","+  doLast {","+    def parserJj = file(\"${project.buildDir}/templates-fmpp/codegen/templates/Parser.jj\")","+    def grammar = parserJj.text","+    calciteParserExtensions.each { anchor, extension ->","+      def count = grammar.count(anchor)","+      if (count != 1) {","+        throw new GradleException(\"Expected '${anchor}' once in Calcite's Parser.jj, found it ${count} times\")","+      }","+      grammar = grammar.replace(anchor, \"${anchor} ${extension}\")","+    }","+    parserJj.text = grammar","+  }"," }"," "," // Generate the FMPP sources from the FMPP templates."],"additions":48,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"sdks/java/extensions/sql/iceberg/src/main/java/org/apache/beam/sdk/extensions/sql/meta/provider/iceberg/IcebergTable.java","lines":["@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@"," package org.apache.beam.sdk.extensions.sql.meta.provider.iceberg;"," "," import static org.apache.beam.sdk.util.Preconditions.checkStateNotNull;","+import static org.apache.beam.vendor.guava.v32_1_2_jre.com.google.common.base.Preconditions.checkArgument;"," "," import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.JsonNode;"," import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.node.ObjectNode;","@@ -25,6 +26,7 @@"," import java.util.List;"," import java.util.Map;"," import java.util.function.IntFunction;","+import 